    "status": "present",
    "value": "A binary string is special when it has as many 1s as 0s and every prefix has at least as many 1s as 0s. Given a special string, you may repeatedly swap two adjacent (consecutive, non-empty) special substrings. Return the lexicographically largest string reachable by such swaps."
  },
